F01,"NASA's planned exploration atmosphere for future vehicles and habitats is 56.5 kPa (8.2 psia) with 34% oxygen, chosen to reduce decompression-sickness risk and shorten spacewalk prebreathe time.",exploration-atmosphere;planning,any,34,34,56.5,56.5,planning,Modeling a 15-min EVA prebreathe protocol using NASA's exploration atmosphere (56.5 kPa/34% O2),https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0094576514004937,2014,Paraphrased from the source text or search excerpt; verify against the source before quoting.,atmosphere,no,,
