F04,"Theory and experimental results indicate that oxygen flammability limits in lunar gravity are lower than those measured in 1g, so materials may burn in lunar habitats at oxygen levels considered safe on Earth.",lunar-gravity;flammability-limit;oxygen,lunar,,,,,review,"Technology development for spacecraft fire safety (FLARE 2021 workshop), NTRS 20210021318",https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210021318,2021,Paraphrased from the source text or search excerpt; verify against the source before quoting.,limit,no,,
F05,"In both 1g and lunar gravity, extinction happens by blow-off. Lower buoyant flow at lunar gravity weakens the flame by reducing oxygen flux but strengthens it by reducing convective heat loss, so the net effect needs measurement.",lunar-gravity;extinction;physics,lunar,,,,,review,"Technology development for spacecraft fire safety (FLARE 2021 workshop), NTRS 20210021318",https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20210021318,2021,Paraphrased from the source text or search excerpt; verify against the source before quoting.,limit,no,,
